 | 0143 | 2026-10-17 | Unlisted products (your request). A product marked **Unlisted** in Shopify was imported as not sellable and showed as Draft, so it vanished from the grid, search and the default Inventory view. **Active and Unlisted** products are now sold and shown; **Draft and Archived** are still kept only for Inventory's status filters. New `src/lib/productStatus.ts` (`parseProductStatus`, `isSellableStatus`) is used by `fetchVariants` in `src/lib/shopify/catalogue.ts` and by Inventory's Active filter; `Variant.status` gains `UNLISTED`, and an unlisted row says *unlisted* under its name. An unrecognised status is treated as not sellable. Needs a catalogue re-import (Settings ▸ Shopify) to fix products already imported. Help pages `stock` and `stock/inventory` updated, `help.json` rebuilt. New `tests/productstatus.test.ts` | your request |
 | 0144 | 2026-10-17 | Scanner keyboard tip (your request, not on the checklist). In any text field except the hidden HID scanner input, when no on-screen keyboard is up (a hardware keyboard or HID scanner is connected) and the field has sat untouched for 4 seconds, a small tip appears under it: "Double-click the scanner trigger to show the keyboard". It goes after 7 seconds or a tap, typing restarts the wait, and tips are at least 90 seconds apart. Not shown in training. `src/lib/scannerKeyboardHint.ts` (timing rules, tested), `src/ui/ScannerKeyboardHint.tsx`, `Field` in `kit.tsx`. Needs your iPad and scanner to confirm the hardware-keyboard detection | - |
 | 0145 | 2026-10-17 | Cart warnings, redesign (your request): **the Customer warning is now the popup itself, not a card inside a sheet.** `CartWarningsSheet.tsx` is a centred popup on phone and tablet (`Sheet` gets a `popup` mode in `kit.tsx` that keeps the open gap, activity and Training layer): the warning's header is the title with a warning icon, the message is the large main text, **For:** is small under it, no inner card, no instruction line, no X. Several warnings are one popup paged like Show: new shared `PageDots` (`kit.tsx`, now also used by Show and Info in `TrainingRun.tsx`, no visible change), **Back** and **Next**, and **Next** becomes **Continue to payment** on the last warning; **Back to cart** is a quiet button on every page. The message area slides a little between pages (off with Reduce Motion) and is as tall as the tallest page so the buttons never move. Tick rules, order, already-seen memory and the call sites are unchanged. New `warning.cancel` spot (Back to cart) and the navgraph edge now taps it (`graph:build` rerun). Help page `sales/cart-warnings`, device test T47 (steps 3, 4 and new 11) and `tests/cartwarnings.test.ts` updated | your request |
+| 0146 | 2026-10-17 | Auto recommended pairs (your request). **Settings ▸ Discounts & bundles**, in a deal's **Recommended pairs**: a new **Auto** button beside **Add a recommended pair**. It pairs variations by **style** (read from the product title, so *Mini Gemstone Dragon* and *Gemstone Egg Dragon (Outer Egg)* are both *gemstone*) and **colour** (the variation title), one variation per position of the deal. Colours are compared as whole sets of words, so *Green* never pairs with *Green Black Dual Colour*; *Black/Red*, *Black & Red* and *Red Black* match. Three passes, strictest first: same words in order, same words in any order, then ignoring *Dual Colour*, *Assorted* and bracketed tags such as *(EOP)*. Each variation is used once per position and unmatched ones are skipped; a note under the buttons gives the count added and names the variations with no match. Pairs already on the deal are kept and their variations are not reused, so Auto only adds. When the groups share no style at all (for example *Highland Cow* with *Tadling*), only colour is compared. New `src/lib/autoPairs.ts` (`autoRecommendedPairs`), `runAuto` in `BundleBuilder.tsx`, new `tests/autopairs.test.ts` (checked against the Python script it came from: same 43 pairs on the dragon deal). Help page `sales/bundles` updated, `help.json` rebuilt. Auto reads names only, so check the list after running it. Not added: an undo for the last Auto run (delete pairs one by one, or use the existing remove buttons) | your request |
 
 
